<% content_for :full_bleed, "1" %>
<% content_for :title, "Security & compliance — Pharma Transport" %>
<% content_for :meta_description, "How Pharma Transport protects the integrity of the chain-of-custody record: hash-chained custody events, mandatory two-factor, static analysis and dependency auditing, and alignment with 21 CFR Part 11 and DSCSA." %>

<section class="bg-brand-900 text-[#eaf0f4]">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-[76px]">
   <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 max-w-[760px]">
    <span class="eyebrow" style="color:#5fb6ac;">Security &amp; compliance</span>
    <h1 class="text-[30px] sm:text-[40px] text-white">The controls behind a record that&rsquo;s meant to survive an audit.</h1>
    <p class="text-[17px] text-[#b9c6d2]">
      Chain-of-custody documentation is only worth as much as its integrity. This is a plain
      account of how the data is protected, how the application is built, and which regulatory
      frameworks the design is aligned to &mdash; including what is not yet claimed.
    </p>
   </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%# Integrity model %>
<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-[76px] border-b border-line">
  <div class="grid gap-14 md:grid-cols-2 items-center">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4">
      <span class="eyebrow">Integrity model</span>
      <h2 class="text-[28px]">Every custody event is hash-chained to the one before it.</h2>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-ink-soft">Each event record stores a cryptographic hash of its own contents plus the hash of the previous event for that batch. Changing a past event &mdash; a time, a location, a signature &mdash; changes its hash, which breaks every link after it. The tampering is detectable; it is not a silent edit.</p>
      <p class="text-[15px] text-ink-soft">Alongside the chain, a separate append-only audit trail records who did what and when, across the whole organization.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="card p-6 bg-[#fbfcfd]">
      <div class="flex flex-col">
        <% [
          ["1", "Pickup — Mesa DC", "hash 9f3c…  prev —"],
          ["2", "Transfer — Phoenix hub", "hash 41ab…  prev 9f3c…"],
          ["3", "Delivery — Tucson, AZ  ✓ signed", "hash c7d0…  prev 41ab…"],
        ].each_with_index do |(n, label, hashes), i| %>
          <% if i > 0 %><div class="w-px h-3.5 bg-line ml-4"></div><% end %>
          <div class="flex gap-3.5 items-center py-3.5">
            <span class="w-[34px] h-[34px] shrink-0 rounded-lg bg-accent-50 text-accent-700 flex items-center justify-center text-[13px] font-semibold"><%= n %></span>
            <div class="flex flex-col">
              <span class="text-[13.5px] font-semibold"><%= label %></span>
              <span class="mono text-[11.5px] text-ink-faint"><%= hashes %></span>
            </div>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%# Controls grid %>
<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-[76px]">
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-2.5 mb-10">
    <span class="eyebrow">Controls</span>
    <h2 class="text-[28px]">How the application itself is secured</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
    <% [
      ["Authentication", [
        "TOTP two-factor authentication, mandatory for admins and pharmacists, opt-in for other roles",
        "One-time backup codes issued at enrollment for device loss",
        "Second-factor secrets encrypted at rest with application-level encryption",
        "Operator reset path for locked-out users, which forces re-enrollment",
      ]],
      ["Application security", [
        "Static analysis (Brakeman) runs on every change in CI",
        "Dependency vulnerability auditing (bundler-audit) on every change",
        "Rate limiting on authentication and sensitive endpoints",
        "Secret scanning on every commit to the repository",
      ]],
      ["Access control & audit", [
        "Policy-based authorization on every action, with per-organization data scoping",
        "Append-only audit trail of user events, visible on the Compliance screen",
        "Custody records hash-chained rather than editable",
      ]],
      ["Billing & data handling", [
        "Payments handled by Stripe; card details never touch our servers",
        "Inbound billing webhooks verified by signature before they are trusted",
        "Hosted on managed infrastructure with encrypted transport (TLS) throughout",
      ]],
    ].each do |heading, items| %>
      <div class="card p-6.5" style="padding:1.625rem;">
        <h3 class="font-sans text-[15px] font-semibold mb-3"><%= heading %></h3>
        <ul class="flex flex-col gap-2">
          <% items.each do |item| %>
            <li class="text-[13.5px] text-ink-soft pl-5 relative">
              <span class="absolute left-0 top-[7px] w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-accent-600"></span><%= item %>
            </li>
          <% end %>
        </ul>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<%# Regulatory alignment %>
<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pb-[76px]">
  <div class="card p-8.5 bg-surface grid gap-9 md:grid-cols-2" style="padding:2.125rem;">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <span class="eyebrow">Regulatory alignment</span>
      <h3 class="text-[20px]">21 CFR Part 11</h3>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-ink-soft">The custody log and generated packets are designed around Part 11&rsquo;s expectations for electronic records: attributable, time-stamped, and protected against undetected alteration, with an independent audit trail.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
      <h3 class="text-[20px]">DSCSA</h3>
      <p class="text-[14px] text-ink-soft">Custody-event logging and per-shipment compliance packets give dispensers an audit-ready record of what happened in transit &mdash; the documentation that matters once the small-dispenser exemption ends on November&nbsp;27,&nbsp;2026. It does not replace a wholesaler&rsquo;s serialization system.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<%# Honest roadmap %>
<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 pb-[84px]">
  <div class="rounded-r border-l-[3px] p-7 flex flex-col gap-2" style="border-color:#b45309;background-color:#fbf1e4;">
    <span class="text-[12px] font-semibold tracking-[0.08em] uppercase text-[#b45309]">What we don&rsquo;t claim yet</span>
    <p class="text-[14px] text-[#5c4420] max-w-[80ch]">
      Pharma Transport is an early-stage product built and run by a single founder. There is
      no SOC&nbsp;2 report or third-party penetration test on file today, and we do not
      currently sign HIPAA business associate agreements. A Compliance Packet is a
      documentation tool &mdash; it is not, on its own, a certification of regulatory
      compliance. If a formal attestation is a procurement requirement for you,
      <%= link_to "tell us", new_user_registration_path %> and we&rsquo;ll be candid about timelines.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="bg-brand-700 text-white">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between gap-8">
    <h2 class="text-[26px] text-white max-w-[24ch]">Have a security questionnaire? Send it over.</h2>
    <div class="flex gap-3">
      <%= link_to "Sign up", new_user_registration_path, class: "btn", style: "background:#fff;color:#1f3a53;" %>
      <%= link_to "See pricing", pricing_path, class: "btn btn-secondary", style: "border-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.3);color:#fff;background:transparent;" %>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
